A||||3||HarryG||Hey rprevo, inquiring minds want to know...||||5||
Z||000000||HarryG||08-29-2000||12:55 PM||||Ray,<BR>Tell us all the gory details on your home-brew SBC swap! A couple questions come to mind:<BR>Since you re-drilled the Fiero flywheel, were there any other mods to it?<BR>How thick is your adapter?<BR>Did you squeeze it all in without cutting any sheetmetal?<BR>TIA!<BR>Harry||||reg||5
Z||000001||rprevo||08-29-2000||05:56 PM|||| My adaptor plate is made out of aluminum<BR>1/2 inch thick. all the dimentions were taken<BR>from the stock Trans and the small block<BR>dims were taken from a bell housing off a<BR>Saginaw trans, To get the data I put the<BR>pieces on a cmm Machine, precision measureing<BR>machine at work, Capable of measuring within<BR>.0002 of an inch.(Your hair on your head is<BR>thicker.) any way made a print, set at the<BR>bridgeport for a few hours and walah!! adaptor plate. My next task was a starter<BR>that could be adjusted with shim, so I made<BR>a block that mounted to my engine that<BR>held the starter, If I replace my starter<BR>and have to shim it I can. I didn't use<BR>a manuel waterpump, I mounted a Morosso electric<BR>pump in place of my spare tire and plumbed<BR>to the front of my block I have no<BR>engine bay modifications except to get<BR>my valve cover off I had to modify one of the<BR>brackets for my trunk lid. For the flywheel<BR>I had to plug some holes put some new<BR>holes in and talk someone in my area into<BR>balanceing it for a 87 and up 1 piece rear<BR>main seal chevy. Alot of balance shops<BR>told me it couldn't be done and I finaly found a guy that said he would try. It's<BR>got 3000 miles on the conversion and<BR>my motor is fine. About 330 horse 350 LT1<BR>converted to Carburator. On that motor the<BR>machining still exists to put a HEI distributer in it.<BR>I'm not in any way knocking the Archie kit<BR>cause not everyone has the access to stuff<BR>that I have. If you can make the stuff it will be a real major job, But a great acomplishment.<P>P.S. I'm a Toolmaker Machine builder in the<BR>Detroit area.<P> Ray  <BR> <BR>   ||||reg||6
Z||000002||redfiero||08-30-2000||06:51 AM||||Anyway I could get a drawing on your adapter?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rprevo||08-30-2000||07:26 AM|||| WE could work something out,<BR>Got any spare parts you might want to<BR>trade?<P>  Ray<P> ||||reg||6
